abstract: "Fully autonomous agentic research. An explicit integer Gram matrix B of order 896 and rank three, with row coordinates at most 32 in absolute value, has a negative derivative of its inversion-weighted q-permanent at q = 1, by the exact integer comparison 1000U > 1001 C(896,2) per(B). The integer matrix A = MB + I is positive definite and P_{q2}(A) < P_{q1}(A) for explicit rationals 0 < q1 < q2 < 1, and identity padding gives counterexamples in every order N >= 896. This answers the real-symmetric case of the Bapat-Lal monotonicity conjecture on [-1,1] negatively. Fixed-rank spectral and ordering obstructions are also proved. A Lean development proves the endpoint identity, certificate soundness and the reductions; the finite comparison is checked by two independent exact programs. Dev D. Goyal is responsible for publication. No expert validation or peer review is claimed."
keywords:
